{"content":[{"c":["BETH-PEOR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Moabite city given to Reuben’s tribe in the partitioning of the Promised Land (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.20","r":"Josh.13.20","rawR":"Josh.13.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.20","value":"Josh.13.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:20"},"). Prior to the Israelites’ entrance into the land of Canaan, they made camp in a valley opposite Beth-peor. Here the people assembled to hear Moses’ final message after he had viewed the land from the top of Mt Pisgah (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.29","r":"Deut.3.29","rawR":"Deut.3.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.29","value":"Deut.3.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.46","r":"Deut.4.46","rawR":"Deut.4.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.46","value":"Deut.4.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:46"},"). It was here that Moses was buried, having been forbidden to enter the territory promised the descendants of Abraham (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.34.6","r":"Deut.34.6","rawR":"Deut.34.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.34.6","value":"Deut.34.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 34:6"},"). Baal-peor (or Baal of Peor) was the name of a local deity worshiped in this region (",{"href":"?bref=Num.25.3-5","r":"Num.25.3-5","rawR":"Num.25.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.25.3-5","value":"Num.25.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 25:3-5"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BethPeor","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 13:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.20","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.20","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.20"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.29","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.29","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.29"},{"anchorText":"4:46","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.46","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.46","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.46"},{"anchorText":"Dt 34:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.34.6","rawQueryValue":"Deut.34.6","sourceRefExact":"Deut.34.6"},{"anchorText":"Nm 25:3-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.25.3-5","rawQueryValue":"Num.25.3-5","sourceRefExact":"Num.25.3-5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"335e08f94070707c9669a4e31bbfc63f0daa3ca4ecf9e86a9423f31b15e87cb5","sourceItemName":"BethPeor","sourceItemOrder":270,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BethPeor","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beth-Peor","title":"Beth-Peor","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}